From: Dict Xiong <me@dxng.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: calibrate pre-E2 PON PCS in USXGMII mode

On an XR1710G with AN7581 E1 silicon, the external WAN PHY negotiates
2.5Gbps but the PON PCS used for its USXGMII connection never obtains
block lock. Manual RX calibration is enabled for the ETH PCS only.

Read the existing pre-E2 calibration requirement for the PON PCS too,
but consume it only for USXGMII Ethernet links. Preserve the existing
ETH policy, PRODUCT_ID < 2 threshold and optical PON calibration paths.
Do not add the separate PON RX-lock recovery callback.

The PON enablement is inspired by the related YYH implementation by
Gilly and Yanghan Ye. This is a scoped adaptation, not a direct
cherry-pick of its E2 calibration and recovery changes.

Enabling this branch for PON USXGMII in the original 6.18.55 kernel
restored the E1 WAN link. Runtime tests covered warm and physical cold
boots, a short peer interface down/up, and native/VID192 IPv4/IPv6
reachability. A kernel rebuilt with this source change has not yet been
boot-tested; other silicon revisions, optical modes and peak throughput
remain untested.

Link: https://github.com/YYH2913/openwrt/commit/fa1edae89eb8765ff6a773a5172bd706a1306503
Signed-off-by: Dict Xiong <me@dxng.cn>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
@@ -1578,11 +1578,11 @@
 	if (IS_ERR(priv->xfi_rst))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(priv->xfi_rst), "failed to get xfi reset lines\n");
 
-	/* For Ethernet PCS, read the AN7581 SoC revision to check if
-	 * manual rx calibration is needed. This is only limited to
-	 * any SoC revision before E2.
+	/* Read the AN7581 revision for pre-E2 manual RX calibration.
+	 * PON calibration is restricted to USXGMII during bring-up.
 	 */
-	if (device_is_compatible(dev, "airoha,an7581-pcs-eth")) {
+	if (device_is_compatible(dev, "airoha,an7581-pcs-eth") ||
+	    device_is_compatible(dev, "airoha,an7581-pcs-pon")) {
 		u32 val;
 
 		ret = regmap_read(priv->scu, AIROHA_SCU_PDIDR, &val);
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
@@ -3219,8 +3219,14 @@
 				   int index, phy_interface_t interface)
 {
 	struct regmap *pcs_pma = priv->pcs_pma[index];
+	bool manual_rx_calib;
 	int calibration_try = 0;
 	u32 val = 0;
+
+	/* Preserve the existing calibration policy for optical PON modes. */
+	manual_rx_calib = priv->manual_rx_calib &&
+		(priv->data->port_type != AIROHA_PCS_PON ||
+		 interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII);
 
 	an7581_pcs_tx_bringup(priv, index, interface);
 	an7581_pcs_rx_bringup(priv, index, interface);
@@ -3230,7 +3236,7 @@
 	usleep_range(100, 200);
 
 retry_calibration:
-	an7581_pcs_cdr_reset(priv, index, interface, priv->manual_rx_calib);
+	an7581_pcs_cdr_reset(priv, index, interface, manual_rx_calib);
 
 	/* Global reset clear */
 	regmap_update_bits(pcs_pma, AIROHA_PCS_PMA_SW_RST_SET,
@@ -3272,7 +3278,7 @@
 	/* Manual RX calibration is required only for SoC before E2
 	 * revision. E2+ SoC autocalibrate RX and only CDR reset is needed.
 	 */
-	if (!priv->manual_rx_calib)
+	if (!manual_rx_calib)
 		return 0;
 
 	/* It was discovered that after a global reset and auto mode gets
